---
import type { LegCurlTopic } from "../../data/leg-curl-topics";

interface Props {
  topic: LegCurlTopic;
}

const { topic } = Astro.props;

const quickFacts = [
  "Leg curls primarily train the hamstrings through knee flexion.",
  "A controlled lowering phase usually increases hamstring tension more than rushing the rep.",
  "For balanced hamstring development, pair leg curls with hip-hinge exercises like Romanian deadlifts.",
];

const relatedLinks = [
  { label: "Leg Curl Machine for Hamstrings", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/for-hamstrings/" },
  { label: "Leg Curl Machine Muscles Worked", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/muscles-worked/" },
  { label: "How to Use a Leg Curl Machine", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/how-to-use-a-leg-curl-machine/" },
  { label: "Common Leg Curl Mistakes", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/common-mistakes/" },
  { label: "Seated vs Lying Leg Curl", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/seated-vs-lying-leg-curl/" },
  { label: "Leg Curl Machine Alternatives", href: "/workouts/leg-curl-machine/alternatives/" },
];
---

<div class="space-y-8">
  <figure class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-hairline">
    <img src={topic.image} alt={topic.imageAlt} class="h-[280px] w-full object-cover sm:h-[420px]" loading="lazy" />
  </figure>

  <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-body">{topic.summary}</p>

  <section class="card border-brand/20 p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Quick facts about {topic.title}</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3 text-body md:grid-cols-3">
      {quickFacts.map((fact) => (
        <li class="rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft p-4">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-brand">Fact</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block">{fact}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Complete guide for people searching {topic.title}</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-body">
      People usually search for {topic.title} when they want to know the right setup, the muscles worked, the benefits, common mistakes, and how to add the movement to a leg day routine. The most important rule is simple: choose a weight you can control, keep your hips stable, and focus on feeling the hamstrings work through the full rep.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-body">
      For most lifters, leg curls work best as an accessory exercise after squats, leg press, lunges, Romanian deadlifts, or other compound lower-body movements. Start with 2–4 sets of 8–15 reps, rest 60–120 seconds, and progress gradually by adding reps before adding weight.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-body"><span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand"></span><span>Use a pad position that feels stable and does not press into the Achilles or knee.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-body"><span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand"></span><span>Curl smoothly, pause briefly, and lower the weight for 2–3 seconds.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2 text-body"><span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand"></span><span>Stop the set if you feel sharp knee, hip, or hamstring pain.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  {
    topic.sections.map((section) => (
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">{section.heading}</h2>
        {section.body && <p class="leading-relaxed text-body">{section.body}</p>}
        {section.bullets && (
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            {section.bullets.map((bullet) => (
              <li class="flex gap-2 text-body">
                <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand"></span>
                <span>{bullet}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <section class="card p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Related leg curl machine guides</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-body">Keep learning with these related guides from the leg workout section.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {relatedLinks.map((link) => (
        <a href={link.href} class="rounded-xl border border-hairline p-4 transition-colors hover:border-brand hover:bg-canvas-soft">
          <span class="block font-semibold text-ink">{link.label}</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block text-sm text-body">Read guide</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-5 sm:p-6">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Safe training note</h2>
    <p class="leading-relaxed text-body">
      Use these guides for education only. Start light, warm up, stop if you feel sharp pain, and consult a qualified professional for injuries or medical conditions.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
